WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.582
These four words appear often in Spark.

00:00:02.582 --> 00:00:05.722
A partition is a chunk of distributed data.

00:00:05.722 --> 00:00:09.192
A task is a unit of work that runs on an executor.

00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:13.947
A stage is a group of tasks that can run before a new exchange is needed.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.537
A shuffle is the movement of data across workers.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:22.342
Shuffles often matter for performance because they require network and disk work.

00:00:22.342 --> 00:00:27.702
Spark distributes work across multiple processes and often multiple machines.

00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:33.672
The driver coordinates the job, while executors perform tasks on partitions of the data.

00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:39.082
This architecture becomes valuable when the data or workload is too large for one machine or when a platform

00:00:39.082 --> 00:00:42.080
needs scalable parallel processing.
